    "result_text": "The build is green \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the derived read-only `riskFlag` field on the Owner response, true when **any** of the three risk signals holds, otherwise false.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`util/DisposableDomains.java`** (new) \u2014 single source of truth for the disposable-domain blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Exposes:\n   - `isBlocked(domain)` \u2014 exact match, used by the existing validator.\n   - `isDisposableAdjacent(email)` \u2014 the softer check: true when the email's *registrable label* (the segment before the public suffix) matches a known disposable domain's, catching lookalikes under a different subdomain or TLD (`inbox.mailinator.com`, `mailinator.net`) that slip past the exact-match block.\n\n2. **`rest/validation/EmailDomainValidator.java`** \u2014 refactored to delegate to `DisposableDomains.isBlocked`, removing the duplicated blocklist. Semantics unchanged.\n\n3. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `@Transient` derived getter `isRiskFlag()`:\n   ```java\n   return this.possibleDuplicate\n       || DisposableDomains.isDisposableAdjacent(this.email)\n       || this.capacityWarning;\n   ```\n   This maps the three spec clauses to existing domain concepts: *possible duplicate* \u2192 the `possibleDuplicate` soft-match flag; *disposable-adjacent email* \u2192 the new util check; *over soft capacity* \u2192 `capacityWarning` (set when the city is at/over the soft threshold of 40, below the hard limit of 50).\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `riskFlag` boolean property (readOnly) with a description documenting the three conditions, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n\n5. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped `riskFlag` via `owner.isRiskFlag()`.\n\nThe one existing acceptance test (`coreRiskFlagFalseNormally`, a fully-unique owner with no email, unique city, no soft-duplicate) correctly reports `riskFlag: false`.\n\nNote: this repo is not a git repository, so there's nothing to commit \u2014 let me know if you'd like me to initialize one.",
