    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change places each piece of logic in the unit this codebase already uses for that kind of work, and it is additive and idiomatic throughout.\n\n- **`isRiskFlag()` on `Owner`** \u2014 Derived read-only DTO fields in this codebase are sourced either as `default` methods on `OwnerMapper` or as derived accessors on the `Owner` model (e.g. `getFiscalYear()`, `getAgeBand()`, `isPossibleDuplicate()`). The aggregation OR's two stored advisory flags plus an email-domain check, so putting it on the model next to `isPossibleDuplicate()`/`isCapacityWarning()` is the natural home. The `@Transient` annotation and `is...` boolean naming match the surrounding derived getters exactly.\n- **Mapper wiring** \u2014 `@Mapping(target = \"riskFlag\", expression = \"java(owner.isRiskFlag())\")` mirrors the existing `fiscalYear` delegation (`owner.getFiscalYear()`), keeping the mapper a thin binding and the logic on the model. Consistent.\n- **`DisposableDomains` util** \u2014 This is a real deduplication win, not a new catch-all. It lifts the previously-inline `BLOCKED_DOMAINS` set out of `EmailDomainValidator` into a single source of truth, and `EmailDomainValidator` now delegates via `isBlocked(...)`. The class matches the established util idiom here (`final` class, private constructor, static methods/constants \u2014 same shape as `RegionTimezones`, `TelephoneNormalizer`, `PostcodeRules`). The two checks it exposes (`isBlocked` for the hard create-time reject, `isDisposableAdjacent` for the soft risk signal) are cohesive and clearly documented, and no competing home for this logic exists in the tree.\n- **OpenAPI** \u2014 The `riskFlag` schema sits with the other `readOnly` derived fields and its description matches the spec.\n\nNo duplication, no unit is becoming a grab-bag, and a maintainer would find each placement natural.",
